cont-in-direct
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-17
what: `Cont.inDirect.shift[A]` — the one-type-argument capture for a
  direct block over Cont's DIAGONAL, taking the answer type from the
  block (`AnswerOf[F]`) as Delim's takes it from its evidence. It gets
  its own scope rather than overloading the package-level `shift`,
  which was tried and refused for a measured reason: a no-type-argument
  call — the shape every handler in the library uses, `shift: k => …`
  in runChoice — resolves to the new overload and then demands a
  DirectCtx. Also: an `import` inside a direct block is an
  "unsupported statement" today, which is what makes the scoped
  spelling unusable; Import statements pass through now.
files: src/main/scala/Cont.scala, src/main/scala/Direct.scala,
  src/test/scala/TestDelimExamples.scala, docs/typepedia.md, CHANGELOG.md
